sections.text:
1. Peacekeepers are granted full policing powers across all Districts.
2. Such powers include, but are not limited to:
   a. Arrest and detention of individuals suspected of violating Capitol law;
   b. Search and seizure of persons, property, and communications;
   c. Establishment of checkpoints, curfews, and restricted zones;
   d. Enforcement of identification and movement controls;
   e. Immediate intervention in any act deemed disruptive to order.
3. No warrant shall be required where action is taken in the interest of Capitol security.

1. Peacekeepers are authorised to use force as necessary to maintain or restore order.
2. Force may be escalated proportionately up to and including lethal force where:
   a. Resistance to Peacekeeper authority is encountered;
   b. A threat to Capitol security or public order is identified;
   c. Compliance cannot be achieved through lesser means.
3. All use of force shall be deemed lawful where undertaken in good faith under this Act.
